From 02923910bf2d4158455a6b8438bcbdb066f43cba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mptfire <263163432+mptfire@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:45:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 21/22] sandbox: sandbox_netns escalates to a true network
 closure

Landlock ABI v4 speaks TCP only, so the base sandbox leaves UDP (DNS
included), ICMP, and abstract Unix sockets open: a sandboxed command
can still exfil through a datagram, and the audit's High #3 was only
TCP-closed. sandbox_netns = true escalates: the child unshares into a
fresh user + network namespace, where the only interface is a downed
loopback, and maps its own uid/gid back through so the filesystem
half keeps working. Nothing datagram-shaped can leave; the probe
sends to a live local listener and hears silence (red-first: with the
flag neutered, the packet arrived).

Same posture as everything here: unprivileged where user namespaces
are allowed, and any refusal fails the spawn instead of degrading
(fail-closed). Opt-in and off by default; the overlay may turn it on
(never off), mirroring sandbox_bash. Config, example, and all three
sandbox construction sites in bootstrap are wired, so worktree tabs
and re-rooted registries inherit the escalation.
